                                dvorakAnywhere

INTRODUCTION

dvorakAnywhere emulates a variant of the German Dvorak Type II on Windows, see
[1] for more information in german. It can be used on public computers, where
you are not allowed to change to your own keyboard layout.

If you are having any problems with dvorakAnywhere (dva) please contact us
using the users mailing list or per e-mail.

USAGE

To use dvorakAnywhere just run the executable. A small window will show up.
From now you can use a variant of the German Dvorak II layout. By killing the
window (e.g. click on [X]) you can stop dvorakAnywhere.

COMPATIBILITY

dva should run on any Windows NT based Operating System (NT, 2000, XP, Vista).
Except from Windows there are no dependencies.

COMPILATION

I compile the binaries using the Gnu C++ Compiler (g++), but any other C++
compiler for Windows should also work.

KNOWN ISSUES

Only works when the keyboard layout is set to german.
Shift and the Numeric Keypad Decimal Operator don't send a dot.

SOURCE CODE ORIGIN

The original source code by Dennis Felsing (r0q) can be downloaded at [2]. I modified it to fix bugs with key up/down events and to enable typing a backtick with the layout.

SPECIAL FEATURES

This fork of dva extends the original dva [2] in two aspects:
  - remaps caps lock to ctrl
  - maps AltGr + 's'/'d' key to <>
  - maps altGR + backtick-key to backtick

[1] http://simon.spruenker.de/dvorak/
[2] https://sourceforge.net/projects/dva/reviews/
